    "body": "## Chat05B review fixes\n\nBase: `main@00ce2baca8dca177dfadffcb8bccbae11bca118f`\nCurrent HEAD: `595532694fb2556637b55b27671237b41d52b7a6`\nThis PR remains Draft and unmerged.\n\n### Finding 1: one authoritative lifecycle state\n\n`gameplay_social_votes` remains the immutable Chat05A trigger/opening record. Its legacy `status='open'` is not the lifecycle authority and is never changed.\n\n`gameplay_social_vote_deadlines` is the sole Chat05B open/closed authority. Closed sidecar state and its terminal tally/choice are immutable. D1 rejects new human and NPC ballots after close. Exact human-ballot replay remains idempotent after close; conflicting choices fail. Repeated result reads return the stored outcome. `gameplay-server/CHAT05B_CONTRACT.md` defines the future Chat05C boundary: it must gate on sidecar `status='closed'`, consume the immutable tally/choice, and must not infer lifecycle state from or mutate the Chat05A row.\n\n### Finding 2: deadline and delayed D1 INSERT\n\nThe implemented cutoff is the trusted Worker timestamp bound immediately before D1 dispatch, checked by the authoritative D1 insert trigger against the immutable deadline. It is **not** a claim that D1 transaction commit occurs before the deadline. The regression uses an explicit hold/release barrier: it captures `D-1`, holds native `.run()`, advances the Worker test clock to `D+1`, confirms release time is at/after D, and only then calls native D1. The saved ballot retains `D-1`; subsequent close includes exactly one human plus six NPC fixture ballots and produces a non-tied quorum-7 result. If the close transaction commits first, the held human insert fails closed.\n\n### Validation on exact HEAD\n\n- Independent critical review: `PASS_CRITICAL_REVIEW`, report `CR461-FINAL-20261031-5955326`, reviewer agent `<HOME>/chat05b_pr461_final_review`. It independently verified the remote tree and all five blob SHAs, examined lifecycle/auth/migration/atomicity and the exact delayed-insert contract, ran SQL post-close probes, 12/12 SQLite tests, and a full local Wrangler/workerd/D1 run (session `47543`).\n- GitHub Actions: all 8 exact-HEAD check-runs succeeded, including both PR and push executions of `private-api-local`, `sqlite-cas`, `wrangler-local-d1`, and `capture`. [PR workflow](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/41169584018), [push workflow](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/41169580000).\n- Local Python SQLite migration/security tests: 12/12 passed. Full local Wrangler/workerd/D1 suite passed, including populated 0011 migration, Chat05A authorization/participant exclusion, quorum matrix 0/1/4/6/7, post-close negatives/replay, close races, rollback/retry, restart and missed-scheduler recovery.\n\nNo Cloudflare deployment or remote D1 migration was performed. No changes to migrations 0001-0010, Chat05C, Chat06, economy, REP, or event logs are included.",
